398	/**
399	 * webpack 4 evaluated every non-harmony module inside a plain function wrapper
400	 * — `function (module, exports, __webpack_require__) { … }` — in the enclosing
401	 * bundle's mode. The bundles create-react-app 3 and 4 emit carry no `"use
402	 * strict"` prologue for those wrappers, so a CommonJS dependency ran in
403	 * sloppy mode: an assignment to an undeclared name silently created a property
404	 * on the global object, and every later reference to that name — in the same
405	 * module or in any other — read it back off the global object.
406	 *
407	 * Vite emits ECMAScript modules, and module code is always strict. The same
408	 * assignment is now a write to an unresolvable reference, which throws
409	 * `ReferenceError: <name> is not defined` the moment the module is evaluated,
410	 * long before the application can mount.
411	 *
412	 * The capability below restores webpack's tolerance without unpicking strict
413	 * mode anywhere. A dependency module that webpack would have wrapped in sloppy
414	 * mode is scanned for exactly the names it assigns without declaring; for each
415	 * one a prelude creates the property on `globalThis` if nothing already holds
416	 * it. Strict mode only rejects assignments to references it cannot resolve, and
417	 * a property of the global object is resolvable, so the original assignment
418	 * evaluates unchanged — and, because the binding lives on the global object
419	 * rather than in the module, cross-module reads of the same name find the same
420	 * value webpack's implicit global gave them.
421	 *
422	 * Three properties matter, and each is enforced rather than asserted:
423	 *
424	 * - Application source is untouched. Only modules under a dependency directory
425	 *   are scanned, so first-party code keeps every strict-mode diagnostic.
426	 * - Harmony modules are untouched. webpack made those strict too, so a module
427	 *   carrying `import`/`export` is left exactly as it is.
428	 * - A module that cannot be analysed is a hard failure naming the module and
429	 *   the diagnostic, never a silent skip.
430	 */
